  ],
  "slug": "cryo-em-66f0",
  "summary": "Recent preprints inject learned mutation priors, pretrained language model embeddings, and template or contact information to guide design and prediction under limited labeled data.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread across these preprints and one peer-reviewed study is the use of an explicit structural or pretrained prior to compensate for limited labeled sequence data. iGC learns a somatic hypermutation prior from B-cell lineage trees and uses it to constrain reinforcement learning for antibody affinity maturation. pLM-bVAE augments a binary variational autoencoder with pretrained protein language model embeddings, reporting improved reconstruction and binary encoding for quantum annealing-based protein sequence design. CARTnet injects template epitope information into contact-aware attention for B-cell epitope prediction, outperforming DiscoTope-3 and BepiPred. MultiMHC fuses RNN sequence features with residue contact graphs for peptide-MHC binding prediction. What is new is treating the form of the prior, whether a mutation model, language model embedding, template, or contact topology, as the explicit lever for performance. The items are heterogeneous in task, spanning design and prediction, so the shared thread is methodological rather than a single application.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-07"
}
